/* book exam traps: A CMRR of 80 dB is a ratio of 10⁴, not 80. Convert with CMRR = 10^(dB/20) before computing common-mode output. | Voltage gain dB uses 20 log₁₀(A); CMRR dB uses 20 log₁₀(Ad/Acm). Both are amplitude ratios; 10 is only for power. | The high-pass removes electrode offset and baseline wander, not 50 Hz mains. Only the notch, or high CMRR with driven right leg, removes mains hum. | The anti-alias filter must be analog and before sample-and-hold. Once aliased, no digital filter can separate it from a real signal. | ADC resolution is VFS/2ⁿ, not VFS/(2ⁿ − 1). 12 bits at 3.3 V gives 0.806 mV per count. */
