/* book Worked example: Q: An ECG is recorded at a paper speed of 25 mm/s with calibration 1 mV = 10 mm. On the strip, the RR interval measures 18 mm and the QRS complex is 2.0 mm wide along the time axis. Find the RR interval in seconds, the heart rate in beats per minute, and the QRS duration in seconds and in milliseconds.
   1. Time scale: 1 mm of paper = 1/25 s = 0.04 s.
   2. RR interval = 18 mm / 25 mm/s = 0.72 s.
   3. Heart rate = 60 / 0.72 s = 83.3 beats per minute.
   4. QRS duration = 2.0 mm / 25 mm/s = 0.08 s.
   5. In milliseconds: 0.08 s × 1000 = 80 ms.
   Answer: RR interval 0.72 s, heart rate 83.3 bpm, QRS duration 0.08 s or 80 ms. */
